    "title": "Purdue outlasts Miami, rolls on to Sweet 16",
    "text": "Yahoo Sports contributor Dalen Cuff reacts to the #2 Boilermakers 79-69 win over the 7-seed Hurricanes and looks ahead to Purdue's matchup with Texas in the West regional.Video TranscriptPurdue prevails.AdvertisementIt wasn't a vintage performance by their lead guard, Braden Smith, who had eight assists, but also eight turnovers in this game.That said, Purdue finds a way to beat Miami by 10. they, they gutted this thing out.Fletcher Loyer, the backcourt mate of Smith that's commonly not discussed, or has been an has had a lot of problems in, in different times this year when they've struggled to win games.He's usually had a poor game.Went off, 24 points, four for four from three.He was excellent at the free throw line late when the issue was still in doubt.So congrats to Purdue.They move on, to the, to the Sweet 16.AdvertisementNow they take on, can't say Cinderella, because they're Texas, but the unexpected 11 seed that's in that situation, a highly talented Texas team.Very interested to see as that line comes out, because Purdue has covered both their games in this tournament.It was a late game situation, but yes, they covered the seven and a half point line here.They're now 12-1 to win the, national championship, 2-1 just to get out of the region.We'll see how that works, because of course Arizona is the number one seed in that region.But first and foremost, they got to beat Texas, and Smith's got to be better for them to do that.",
